able general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Kevin Hern (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Kevin Hern's retirement leaves this Tulsa-area seat open, but the district's strong Republican fundamentals make a Democratic takeover unlikely. Mark Tedford enters the general election with a massive fundraising advantage, having raised roughly $2.5 million to John Croisant's $217,000, along with about $95,000 in outside support and former President Trump's endorsement after his rival's runoff withdrawal.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on the district's R+11 partisan lean, the favorable Republican environment, and a unanimous expert consensus rating the race Solid or Safe R. Prediction markets likewise give Croisant only about a 7% chance. A Republican hold by a double-digit margin is the clear expectation, though the absence of polling keeps some uncertainty around the exact size of the win.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0439, "margin": -11.04}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0097, "margin": -18.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0191, "margin": -15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.0497, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0244, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0398, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.05, "margin": -12.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.0401, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.0392, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.0141, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.021, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.0228, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.033, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.0238, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.0259, "margin": -13.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.0198, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.0096, "margin": -14.0}, {"date": 